{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# S4: Config-driven link-relation mapping, skip-not-approximate preserved\n\n## Context / Problem\n\nEpic 3d7a adds a config-driven mapping seam. S1 landed core `mapping_config.py`\n(`MappingLayer` with `link_map: Mapping[str,str]`, `SKIP=\"skip\"`,\n`resolve_for_project`, `validate`, `Capability`). S2 made STATUS config-driven\n(`config.effective_status_map`, `config.py:77`). S4 does the same for\nrebar-relation → Jira-link mapping while preserving \"skip, don't approximate\": map\nto a real declared project link type, or skip — never invent an approximate link.\n\nLink emission has TWO symmetric halves in `outbound_links.py`, both reached only\nfrom the UPDATE path (`outbound_mutation_builders.py:285`; creates emit no links):\n\n- ADD — `_diff_links` (`outbound_links.py:34`): per local dep, calls\n  `links.link_payload_for_relation(relation)` (`:83`) and skips when it returns\n  `None` (`:84`).\n- REMOVE — `_diff_link_removals` (`outbound_links.py:120`): walks the remote\n  canonical set `links.map_remote_links(jira_fields)` (entries `(relation,\n  other_key, opaque_vendor_type)`), and for a managed-but-locally-absent link emits\n  `{\"action\":\"remove\",\"type\":opaque_vendor_type,...}` (`:150`). It exists to stop\n  the inbound differ re-adding a deliberate local unlink every pass (the churn).\n\nBoth `link_payload_for_relation` impls read the built-in `RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`\ndirectly, in TWO backends: `adapters/jira/backend.py:323` (import `:29`) and\n`adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:527` (import `:26`).\n\nBuilt-in `RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK: dict[str, tuple[str, bool]]`\n(`adapters/jira_family/value_maps.py:104`): `blocks→(Blocks,False)`,\n`depends_on→(Blocks,True)`, `relates_to→(Relates,False)`. Unsynced relations:\n`UNSYNCED_RELATIONS` (`value_maps.py:128`: duplicates, supersedes, discovered_from,\ncaused_by). TYPE MISMATCH to reconcile: built-in payload is a `(link_type, swap)`\nTUPLE; the S1 `link_map` axis is flat `str→str` (`mapping_config.py:98`). Parent\nrelationships are OUT of scope (S7).\n\n## Approach\n\nMirror S2's forward seam, and apply ONE effective link map SYMMETRICALLY to both\nthe ADD and REMOVE paths.\n\n1. **New `config.effective_link_map(project_key, root)`** (`config.py`, NEW),\n   analogous to `effective_status_map` (`config.py:77`). Add an adapter-free literal\n   `local_to_jira_link: dict[str,str]` = `{\"blocks\":\"Blocks\",\"depends_on\":\"Blocks\",\n   \"relates_to\":\"Relates\"}` (link-TYPE component only; kept honest by a parity test,\n   like `local_to_jira_status`). Build `builtin = mc.MappingLayer(\n   link_map=local_to_jira_link)`, resolve via `mc.resolve_for_project`, then\n   `mc.validate(resolved, mc.Capability(has_link_types=True))` (fail-closed) and\n   return `resolved.link_map`, **retaining `SKIP` entries** (unlike status) so a\n   forced skip is distinguishable from an absent key.\n\n2. **One resolver, both directions.** Add `_effective_link_map_for(ticket, mapping,\n   repo_root)` in `outbound_differ.py` (NEW, sibling of `_effective_status_map_for`,\n   `:272`). Compute it once at `outbound_mutation_builders.py:285` and pass the SAME\n   `link_map: Mapping[str,str] | None = None` to BOTH `_diff_links` and\n   `_diff_link_removals` (new arg on each). Add a shared helper\n   `_resolve_link(relation, links, link_map) -> tuple[str, bool] | None` used by both\n   so the rule cannot diverge between directions.\n\n3. **Reconciliation rule (`_resolve_link`, tuple ↔ string):**\n   - `override = link_map.get(relation)` (None when no config / absent key).\n   - `override == SKIP` → return `None` (skip).\n   - `payload = links.link_payload_for_relation(relation)`.\n   - `override` is a `str` → return `(override, payload[1] if payload else False)` —\n     config overrides ONLY the link_type; the built-in swap is preserved (`swap=False`\n     default for a newly-mapped unsynced relation).\n   - else → return `payload` (may be `None` → skip).\n\n   **ADD** (`_diff_links`): use `_resolve_link`; `None` ⇒ `continue`; else emit\n   `type=vendor_type, swap=swap`.\n\n   **REMOVE** (`_diff_link_removals`): for each canonical `(relation, other_key,\n   opaque_vendor_type)`, `relation is None` stays skipped (unmapped → inbound adopt);\n   otherwise call `_resolve_link(relation, ...)`:\n   - `None` (SKIP or unmapped) ⇒ **`continue` — suppress the REMOVE.** A skipped\n     relation is neither added NOR removed; removing it would let inbound re-add it,\n     the exact churn this pass prevents.\n   - `(vendor_type, _swap)` ⇒ emit `type=vendor_type` (the OVERRIDE when remapped),\n     so add/remove reference ONE resolved link type, never built-in vs override.\n\n   With no `[mapping]` block both paths are byte-for-byte today's behaviour.\n\n4. **Fail-closed on undeclared link type.** The S1 mechanism exists\n   (`MappingLayer.link_types` `mapping_config.py:102`, `Capability.has_link_types`\n   `:80`, `validate()`'s `_check_vocab(resolved.link_map, resolved.link_types)`\n   `:359`) but `validate()` is not yet invoked. A project declares\n   `[mapping.default] link_types = [...]`; `effective_link_map` calling `validate()`\n   (NEW) raises `MappingConfigError` on any `link_map` value outside it. `SKIP`\n   always allowed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `config.py`: `local_to_jira_link` literal + `effective_link_map` (~100→~130 LOC).\n- `outbound_differ.py`: `_effective_link_map_for`.\n- `outbound_links.py`: `link_map` arg + shared `_resolve_link` helper on BOTH\n  `_diff_links` and `_diff_link_removals` (178→~215 LOC).\n- `outbound_mutation_builders.py`: compute + pass `link_map` at `:285`.\n- Backends UNCHANGED (built-in payload stays; config layers above both).\n- NEW `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_link_mapping.py`.\n- OUT of scope: parents (S7), inbound remap-awareness, priority/type axes.\n- All touched modules stay well under the 800-LOC hard cap.\n\n## Testing\n\nNew `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_link_mapping.py` (`pytestmark =\npytest.mark.unit`), driving REAL entry points (`config.effective_link_map`,\n`_diff_links`, `_diff_link_removals`) via a tmp `rebar.toml` `[mapping]` block;\nobservable behaviour only:\n\n- `test_link_config_effect` — a `link_map` override (e.g. `relates_to =\n  \"Relationship\"`) changes the ADD mutation's `type` while preserving the built-in\n  `swap`; AND, on the REMOVE path, a managed-but-absent remapped link emits a remove\n  whose `type` is the OVERRIDDEN link type (add/remove share one type). No\n  `[mapping]` ⇒ both paths unchanged.\n- `test_link_skip_preserved` — a `\"skip\"` override (and an unsynced relation) emits\n  NO ADD; AND the SAME skip override suppresses the REMOVE (no remove mutation),\n  proving neither add nor remove for a skipped relation. No approximate link ever\n  substituted.\n- `test_link_undeclared_fails_closed` — a `link_map` value outside a declared\n  `link_types` vocabulary makes `effective_link_map` raise `MappingConfigError`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The SAME effective `link_map` governs ADD and REMOVE via one `_resolve_link`\n      helper; `_diff_links` ADD composes override link_type + built-in swap;\n      verified by `test_link_config_effect`.\n- [ ] \"Skip, don't approximate\" is symmetric: a `\"skip\"` override (and unsynced\n      relations) suppress BOTH the ADD and the REMOVE, so a skipped relation is never\n      added nor removed (no inbound re-add churn); verified by\n      `test_link_skip_preserved`.\n- [ ] A remapped relation's REMOVE targets the overridden link type (add/remove\n      reference one resolved type); verified by `test_link_config_effect`.\n- [ ] Undeclared link type fails closed against declared `link_types` via\n      `validate()`; verified by `test_link_undeclared_fails_closed`.\n- [ ] Both consumers (`adapters/jira/backend.py:323`,\n      `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:527`) route through the single\n      `effective_link_map` seam; no `[mapping]` block leaves emission unchanged.\n- [ ] A parity test keeps `config.local_to_jira_link` in lock-step with\n      `value_maps.RELATION_TO_JIRA_LINK`'s link-type components.\n\nTest tier: unit"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787354731919077001,"uuid":"0269b242-5b91-4a3a-96ab-d3a52c904183"}